      "MONICA: Well, my dears, I'm sure I can say on behalf of Mrs Blaney, as well as myself, that it's moments like this that make our little efforts here…\nMRS DAVISSON: You mean you just don't do it for the money ?\nMONICA: — ; Of course, Mrs Davisson, this is a business, and financial considerations prevail but our ultimate satisfaction is at the making of two …\nMRS DAVISSON: Nice of you, Miss Barling. Keep up the good work., |",
      "BRENDA: Monica, dear, it's nearly four-thirty. Why don't you take the rest of the afternoon off? I'm sure there's some shopping you'd like to do.\nMONICA: Well, thank you, Mrs Blaney ... if you're sure you don't need me.\nBRENDA: I'm quite sure thank you. Good night."
